a, Joe Henry, Daniel Lanois y Bob Mould.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":69995569990107,"artist":"Melissa Etheridge","artist_id":138312728338476,"title":"Melissa Etheridge","year":1988,"ess":0,"yt":"pV8_o4RJc7s","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,184,null]]},{"id":131621234121380,"artist":"Melissa Etheridge","artist_id":138312728338476,"title":"Bring Me Some Water","year":null,"ess":0,"yt":"oIvXUNp8HtU","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los ochenta","scene_id":13391632264459,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-80s","chapters":["Sección 5.16"],"pages":[[1,184,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":184,"text":"…(1988), conquered the air-waves and made it popular for young women to sing about their psyches. Los Angeles boasted the most prolific school. Melissa Etheridge (1988), the debut by Melissa Etheridge (1), was wild and passional, and her delivery was the closest to Janis Joplin's of any acoustic folksinger, especially in gospel and r&b-infected…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":69995569990107,"type":"album","name":"Melissa Etheridge","list_id":115932688871073,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Heartland Rock","src":"musthear","rank":80,"year":1988,"note":null,"yt":"pV8_o4RJc7s","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":69995569990107,"type":"album","name":"Melissa Etheridge","list_id":52032266791182,"list":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","rank":558,"year":1988,"no